course: dictionary
lesson: 12602
title: A formal word for an awkward feeling
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are long and formal, but you can often work them out from the clues around them. «To her discomfiture, she forgot her lines in the school play.» Her lines are the words she has to say on stage. Forgetting them is awkward, and the whole class might be watching, so discomfiture must be an embarrassed, uneasy feeling.
explain: «Everyone laughed, and Sam's cheeks turned red.» Red cheeks show that Sam is embarrassed. Laughing at him makes the feeling worse. Discomfiture is the name for that awkward feeling when you look foolish in front of others.
explain: Discomfiture can also be an old word for a plan that fails. «The general's plan failed, and his discomfiture was plain to all.» Here the plan went wrong, so his discomfiture means defeat. When you read an old book, check which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: Discomfiture is a noun, so it names a feeling or a state.
fact: Discomfiture means embarrassment and unease when someone is confused or made to look foolish.
fact: In older writing, discomfiture can also mean defeat or failure of a plan.
fact: You will often see the phrases «to his discomfiture» and «much to her discomfiture» in classic books.
fact: Discomfiture is a formal word, so you will mostly find it in books and serious writing, not in everyday chat.
exercise: «To her discomfiture, she forgot her lines in the school play.» What does discomfiture mean here? | A loud cheer from the crowd | Great joy and pride | A new pair of shoes | *Embarrassment and unease
exercise: «Everyone laughed, and Sam's cheeks turned red.» Which clue shows that Sam feels discomfiture? | The sun was shining | *His cheeks turned red after everyone laughed | Everyone cheered for him | Sam won the race
exercise: «The general's plan failed, and his discomfiture was plain to all.» In this old sense, what does discomfiture mean? | Building a new bridge | A soft, gentle breeze | *Failure of a plan | A big party with music
test: Which feeling is discomfiture? | *Awkward and embarrassed | Calm and relaxed | Sleepy and bored | Proud and brave
test: Fill in the gap: «Much to his ___, the magician's rabbit ran off the stage.» | Delight | *Discomfiture | Hunger | Kindness
exam: Which sentence uses discomfiture correctly? | «The sun rose early over the hills.» | «They painted the fence bright blue.» | *«Much to his discomfiture, the whole class saw him fall off his chair.» | «He ate a big sandwich for his lunch.»
